================================================================================
TRANSITION PHASE: ABOUT -> PROJECTS (The VR Portal)

Vibe: Leaving the volatile, heavy engine room and stepping into a clean,
suspended, high-pressure aerodynamic space.
Goal: Execute a massive paradigm shift in color and mechanics by using a
scroll-locked 3D/SVG morph sequence, transitioning the user from the "Fire"
era to the "Air" era.

SCROLL MECHANICS (The Timeline Lock)

This transition requires "Scroll-Jacking" to orchestrate the animations
perfectly without the user scrolling past them.

Container Setup: A position: relative wrapper with a large height
(e.g., height: 300vh).

Viewport Lock: A position: sticky; top: 0; height: 100vh; child element
that holds the visuals. As the user scrolls down the 300vh container,
the visuals stay pinned to the screen, and the scroll progress (0% to 100%)
drives the animation timeline below.

STAGE 1: THE AIRLOCK (0% - 25% Scroll Progress)

The transition begins by extinguishing the "Fire" elements.

Heat Dissipation: The ambient orange radial gradient from the bottom of the
About section gets rapidly blown away downwards.

Cursor Detachment:

The "Plasma Shooter" custom cursor immediately detaches from the user's
mouse coordinates.

It animates via an ease-out curve to the exact dead center of the viewport.

The user's mouse reverts to a standard pointer.

Background: Remains #0F172A (Deep Matte Slate) during this phase.

STAGE 2: THE MORPH (25% - 60% Scroll Progress)

The artifact transforms to bridge the timeline from the 2100s to the Modern era.

The Transformation:

The centralized Plasma Shooter graphic scales up slightly and begins
a rapid rotation (e.g., flipping 180 degrees on the Y-axis).

During the rotation, the SVG path morphs (or the WebGL model swaps)
from the volatile weapon into a sleek, silver, minimalist VR Headset.

Visual Cue: As the headset locks into place facing the user, a subtle glowing
chamfered edge (CSS box-shadow or Canvas glow) traces the outline of
the headset's lenses, indicating it is a portal.

STAGE 3: THE DIVE (60% - 95% Scroll Progress)

The user is forced "inside" the headset.

The Zoom: The VR Headset scales exponentially (transform: scale(1) to scale(50)).
The camera appears to push directly into the glowing lenses.

The Color Inversion (The Flash):

As the edges of the VR lenses expand past the boundaries of the user's monitor,
the background color undergoes a rapid, hard transition.

#0F172A (Deep Matte Slate) instantly flashes to #F8FAFC (Light Slate).

Wind Tunnel Effect:

Faint, fast-moving horizontal speed-lines (using a lightweight Canvas
particle emitter) shoot past the camera, establishing the "Air" and
aerodynamic physics of the next section.

STAGE 4: PARALLAX HAND-OFF (95% - 100% Scroll Progress)

The lock is released, and the user has fully arrived in the Projects section.

Physics Initialization: The dangling Project cards drop into the viewport from
the top, bouncing slightly on their invisible spring constraints.

Control Return: The scroll lock ends (position: sticky hits the bottom of
its wrapper). The user resumes normal vertical scrolling, but they are now
navigating inside the "fake 3D" parallax space of the Modern Gallery.

TECHNICAL UX & PERFORMANCE NOTES

Cleanup: The moment the screen flashes to white (#F8FAFC) at Stage 3, you
MUST unmount the Heat Haze DOM nodes and the border-melting <feDisplacementMap>
filters from the About section. Leaving them active off-screen will severely
tank the framerate of the spring physics in the upcoming Projects section.

Animation Engine: Use a library like GSAP ScrollTrigger to map the scroll
progress to the scale, morph, and color inversion properties effortlessly.